!! Testimony ~ Yin-Luna, wave two (verbatim)

```text
<<~ status "Yin-Luna: wave-two ratchet complete; one Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above faces; same-process isolation remains a LEAD" >>

# Yin-Luna · Lares (Tasked Spirit) · Persona: Ink-Clerk

Sources below were read 2026-10-18; repository paths are relative to `/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine`. “Own” means Yin’s wave-one claim; “twin” means Yang’s. The framing ruling is the governing target, not evidence that the implementation meets it.

## Claims ledger

| Claim | Origin | Finding | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| Today a vessel Keyhive identity registers all bags supplied to boot, and is seeded from vessel seed. | both | CONFIRMED | `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:95-101,185-188` |
| Face founding makes a veil identity and a PersonaGroup under it; vessel and veil use the same replayed event store. | both | CONFIRMED | `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/ceremony-core.ts:343-370` |
| Each face already has its own archive slot/row, while vessel archive remains too. | both | CONFIRMED | `packages/lararium-node/src/identity-anchors.ts:124-169`; `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-keyhive-archive.ts:18-31,69-94` |
| Registration is a union over all fleet memberships; a session needs exactly one face and a face-local registry. | twin / own | CONFIRMED (current union); target is the 2026-10-18 ruling | `packages/lararium-mesh/src/register-bags.ts:84-119`; roadmap `stable-founding-road.mem:106-109` |
| Face group removal rolls reached bags; founder identity cannot leave its own group, so fresh group is the ruling/lean. | both | CONFIRMED as house design; K12 remains owed implementation | `kapae.mem:234,272`; `sealed-store.mem:357`; roadmap `stable-founding-road.mem:598,751` |
| Carried bag events expose creator in clear; this is a measured privacy leak, not merely inference. | twin / own | CONFIRMED | roadmap `stable-founding-road.mem:486` (measured probe, 2026-10-16); `ceremony-core.ts:350-355` |
| Herm can boot at floor without face pins, receiving fewer caps. | both | CONFIRMED | `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:109-124` |
| Per-face restore should carry only that face’s archive, group and key memory; current code already guarantees this. | twin | LEAD in the first clause as desired architecture; REFUTED as a current guarantee: vessel-wide shared store/provider and key holder remain | `operator-daemon-behavior.ts:971-1002,1043-1054`; per-face archive paths above. Exact event/key isolation needs wiring and probe. |
| Multiple Keyhive providers can safely coexist in one WASM process with separate identities/stores. | twin / own | LEAD | Keyhive Rust `keyhive/keyhive_core/src/keyhive.rs:85-132` holds maps/stores on each object; local provider calls `KH.Keyhive.init` at `keyhive-provider.ts:190-255`. No cited source promises WASM runtime isolation or independent mutable globals. |
| Keyhive alpha is production/security audited. | twin | REFUTED (implicit safety implication) | pinned `packages/lararium-keyhive/package.json`; `keyhive/README.md:8-18` calls source pre-alpha, warns against production and says unaudited. |
| Current architecture has one face identity per PersonaGroup and none above. | framing | REFUTED | vessel Keyhive still boots and registers at `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts:95-101,185-188`; veil is separate at `operator-daemon-behavior.ts:994-1002`; shared event store at `:973,997`. |

## Converged story × vessel

| Story | Node | Browser |
|---|---|---|
| Two faces/tabs and private book | One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup; each tab/session proves exactly one face. Content-key seat, event store, registry and archive scoped to that group. | Same; separate face contexts within one vessel keystore. Current vessel identity, union registration and shared event stream can correlate; W25 creator cleartext is a demonstrated leak. |
| Remove phone from work only | Signed causal dyad/removal in work fleet; roll work group’s reached bag keys only. Elyncia seat/keys remain. Founder seat requires fresh group. | Same causal semantics across tabs; no clock expiry. |
| Faceless herm | Floor/place identity only if transport requires it; no face capability, groups or registration. | No face session/capability; floor only. |
| Restore one face | Bundle selects one group archive, event slice, and that face’s key memory; restored devices rejoin only that PersonaGroup. | Restore one face row and rejoin that face; never import sibling state. Current archive rows alone do not prove event/key isolation. |
| Sibling joins | Admit its device root to the selected face group; no sibling group or bags. | Same; tab unlock is per face. |
| Migration | Remove vessel Individual from cap identity; split event history and content-key/archive custody by face; re-register each face catalog under its own Keyhive identity. | Same, with per-face archive rows already named but require correct isolated contents and ownership. |
| One process / Keyhive alpha | Per-object Rust maps imply an API shape for multiple providers, not a safety guarantee. Probe wasm globals, signers, stores and concurrent callbacks. | Same probe; do not ship an isolation claim until it passes. |

**Where my mind changed:** I had treated “several providers in one runtime” as a plausible implementation route from instance fields. Yang made the same inference. The actual Rust object confirms instance-owned maps, but neither that nor `Keyhive.init` establishes WASM-level isolation; I now hold that as unresolved. Both faces also agree archive rows are already face-named; I narrow my earlier concern: names are per-face, but archive contents, event store and content-key seats are still wired with vessel-wide assumptions.

## Build order both faces can stand behind

1. **Face context and isolated stores.** Introduce a context keyed by PersonaGroup; isolate event store, registry, archive and key seat. Red: write/emit in A, prove B and floor cannot list/replay/open it; restart A and B independently.
2. **Identity and founding.** Face Keyhive founds/owns group and card; remove above-face Individual from face traffic. Red: capture event bytes/cards from A and B; fail if any stable vessel/ancestor identity links them. Restore only A and verify membership/prekeys.
3. **Session and registration routing.** Derive registry per selected face; route each bag directly to its owner. Red: A cannot resolve/register B URI; private-book packet contains no B or vessel identity.
4. **Causal removal and founder succession.** Per-face roll; founder removal via fresh group and re-seat standing devices. Red: remove work phone, count causal raise, assert work content rotates and Elyncia access remains; quiet replica/clock skew never removes.
5. **Herm, restore and wire audit; fence.** Floor-only herm; face-only bundles; migrate/re-found without cross-face compatibility shim before second operator. Red: herm has no face caps; restored A cannot list B; old mixed archive refuses clearly; W25 creator privacy probe passes.

## Standing disagreements and probes

- **Same-process multi-instance:** source shows object-local state, but whether WASM/runtime has mutable shared state is unresolved. Probe two providers with distinct signers/stores under concurrent operations, reboot/replay, and cross-read attempts; if any state crosses, isolate in workers/processes.
- **Archive/event split sufficiency:** both favor per-face persistence; current code reuses daemon event store. Probe packet/storage and restore B after writing only A; require no A identifiers/events/keys accessible or linkable.
- **Faceless place key:** both lean transport-only floor identity where protocol needs it. Probe that it cannot author, resolve or observe face caps; otherwise retain no Keyhive identity.

## Operator-owned forks (current lean → what flips it)

- **Place identity:** retain transport-only floor key → remove it if a herm can operate and route without one; never grant face caps.
- **Runtime isolation:** same process only after probe → choose per-face workers if shared mutable WASM state or callbacks cross.
- **Legacy migration:** fresh identities/groups for co-mingled histories, no bridge before fence → preserve an old identity only with evidence its history/archive was face-exclusive and unlinkable.
- **Founder removal:** fresh PersonaGroup is the clean path → change only if substrate gains a verified authority path that removes the founder and demonstrably rolls every reached bag.
- **At-rest portability:** sealed per-face rows are the lean → operator chooses a portable recovery format if device-to-device restore requires it; it must still carry one face only.

